---
import {productionBook,inheritedSize,MAKING_PATHS} from '../../lib/studio/productionBook';
const {project,cards=[],sections=[]}=Astro.props;
const initial={book:productionBook(project.settings??{},project.deck_type),size:inheritedSize(project.settings??{}),cards:cards.map((c:any)=>({id:c.id,title:c.title,version_number:c.version_number})),sections:sections.map((s:any)=>({id:s.id,title:s.title,version_number:s.version_number})),updatedAt:project.updated_at};
---
<section data-chapter-panel="making" class="chapter-making" hidden data-making>
<script type="application/json" data-making-initial set:html={JSON.stringify(initial).replaceAll('<','\\u003c')}/>
<nav class="making-moments" aria-label="The Making moments">{['My making path','The experience','Production partners','Prepare the edition','Proof and decision','Production Book'].map((s,i)=><button type="button" data-making-step={i}>{s}</button>)}</nav>
<div data-making-panel="0"><p class="studio-eyebrow">Section seven · The Making</p><h2>What does finished look like for your deck?</h2><p>A handmade gift, a small printed edition or a digital experience can all honor your idea. Begin with the experience you want to create; the path can change.</p><label>Edition name<input data-making-field="name" placeholder="For example: a first personal edition"/></label><label>My making path<select data-making-path><option value="">Still exploring</option>{Object.entries(MAKING_PATHS).map(([value,name])=><option value={value}>{name}</option>)}</select></label><label>What finished means for this edition<textarea data-making-field="finished" rows="4"/></label><p class="making-note">One working edition is supported here. Selecting multiple formats records your intention; it does not create separate editions or duplicate the deck.</p></div>
<div data-making-panel="1" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The physical or digital experience</p><h2>How should it feel to use?</h2><p>Think about handling, reading, durability and the moment of opening or accessing your deck.</p><aside class="making-size"><strong>Existing deck-wide size</strong><p data-making-size/><button type="button" data-chapter="visual-world" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary">Review my deck design</button><p>This chapter inherits that choice. Changing the size belongs in deck design, where the artwork implications can be reviewed.</p></aside><label>Quantity or digital delivery intention<input data-making-field="quantity"/></label><label>Materials, finish and handling<textarea data-making-field="materials" rows="4"/></label><details><summary>Guidebook and packaging decisions — optional until ready</summary><p>Leave these undecided while the deck develops. These are planning choices, not a printer compatibility check.</p><label>Planned number of cards<input data-making-field="plannedCardCount" inputmode="numeric" placeholder={project.deck_type==='tarot'?'78 is the usual tarot starting point':'Undecided'}/></label><p>Tarot usually starts with 78 cards; additional creator cards are welcome. This count does not assign printed numbers or choose a tarot tradition. Extra cards are not automatically numbered 78 or 79.</p><label>Guidebook delivery<select data-making-field="guidebookDelivery"><option value="">Undecided</option><option value="digital">Digital</option><option value="printed">Printed</option><option value="both">Digital and printed</option></select></label><label>Cards packaging<select data-making-field="packagingType"><option value="">Undecided</option><option value="cards-only">Cards only</option><option value="tuck">Tuck box</option><option value="sleeve">Sleeve</option><option value="rigid">Rigid box</option><option value="other">Other — describe below</option></select></label><label>Printed guidebook placement<select data-making-field="bookPlacement"><option value="">Undecided</option><option value="boxed-with-cards">Boxed with the cards</option><option value="separate">Supplied separately</option><option value="not-applicable">No printed guidebook</option></select></label><label>Book page count, paper and estimated thickness<input data-making-field="bookThickness" placeholder="Undecided — confirm with the printer"/></label><label>Fit, dependencies and supplier confirmation<textarea data-making-field="fitNotes" rows="3"/></label><p>Check final card count and stock thickness, card size, book dimensions and thickness, and internal box clearance together. A digital-only book with a boxed printed book choice needs review. Changing any part can affect the fit.</p><details><summary>? What has the printer confirmed?</summary><p>MPC lists 10–160 cards for its 70 × 121 mm tarot product, not a general 82-card limit. That range does not confirm every count, stock, booklet and box combination. Confirm the exact configuration and physical sample with your chosen supplier.</p><a href="https://www.makeplayingcards.com/design/design-your-own-tarot-cards.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MPC tarot product specifications</a></details><label>Companion format<textarea data-making-field="companion" rows="3"/></label><label>Packaging or digital presentation<textarea data-making-field="packaging" rows="3"/></label><label>Material values and accessibility<textarea data-making-field="values" rows="3"/></label></details></div>
<div data-making-panel="2" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Production partners</p><h2>Ask the questions that matter.</h2><p>Compare the same specifications, including samples, proofs, freight, taxes, terms and delivery. A lower unit price may not mean a lower delivered cost.</p><label>Supplier options, questions and reasons<textarea data-making-field="partners" rows="6"/></label><details><summary>Costs and delivery assumptions</summary><label>Budget, quotation dates, inclusions and exclusions<textarea data-making-field="costs" rows="4"/></label><label>Delivery, inspection and handover notes<textarea data-making-field="delivery" rows="4"/></label></details><p>No supplier is contacted and no order or payment is placed from this Section.</p></div>
<div data-making-panel="3" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Preparing this edition</p><h2>Keep a clear record of the material you mean.</h2><p>Choose cards and companion sections, then record their current versions alongside these edition decisions. Later writing changes do not alter an earlier record.</p><div data-making-sources/><label>Rights, credits and permissions still to verify<textarea data-making-field="rights" rows="4"/></label><label>Open questions and explicit exceptions<textarea data-making-field="outstanding" rows="4"/></label><p><strong>Working image previews are not print-ready originals.</strong> Check full-quality artwork, supplier-specific trim/bleed/safe areas, color, resolution, orientation and permissions separately.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-making-capture>Record this package's source versions</button><p>This creates a private reference record, not a folder of production files or a submission to a printer.</p></div>
<div data-making-panel="4" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The proof and the decision</p><h2>Review a proof and record your decision</h2><div data-making-review/><label>The recorded package I reviewed<select data-making-proof-package></select></label><label>Proof reviewed<select data-making-proof-kind><option value="not-reviewed">Not reviewed yet</option><option value="digital">Digital proof</option><option value="physical">Physical sample or proof</option></select></label><label>My decision<select data-making-proof-decision><option value="pause">Pause</option><option value="revise">Request revisions</option><option value="accept">Accept this proof with recorded conditions</option></select></label><label>What I reviewed, corrections and remaining conditions<textarea data-making-proof-notes rows="5"/></label><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-making-proof>Record my proof decision</button><p>This is an internal record about a specific proof. It does not certify the deck, authorize manufacturing, accept supplier terms or place an order.</p></div>
<div data-making-panel="5" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">My Production Book</p><h2>Keep the decisions behind the finished work.</h2><p>Revisit your notes, recorded versions and proof decisions as this edition develops.</p><div data-making-book/><details class="studio-local-recovery"><summary>Recover unsaved work</summary><p>Keep a local copy of current editor state. Normal saved outputs are in Exports.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-making-download>Recover current Production Book notes</button></details><p>This readable planning export includes current unsaved notes. Complete project backups retain the underlying settings and history; this chapter does not replace your original production assets.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-chapter="into-the-world">Explore Into the World</button></div>
<div class="making-actions"><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-making-save>Save my Production Book</button><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-making-next>Continue</button></div><p data-making-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Private edition planning. No production approval is implied.</p>
</section>
<script>import '../../scripts/chapterMaking';</script>
<style>.chapter-making h2{font:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem)/1.2 'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif}.chapter-making p{line-height:1.7}.making-moments{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.3rem;font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.making-moments button{border:0;background:none;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;padding:.5rem .3rem;font:inherit;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}.making-moments button[aria-current]{border-color:#5c735a;font-weight:600}.chapter-making label{display:grid;gap:.5rem;margin:1.2rem 0;font-weight:600}.chapter-making input,.chapter-making select,.chapter-making textarea{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;padding:.75rem;font:400 1rem/1.6 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;background:white;border:1px solid #9d9e94;border-radius:3px;color:#242b2b}.chapter-making textarea{resize:vertical}.making-illustration{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin:1rem 0}.making-note{font-size:.85rem;color:#58605d}.making-size{padding:1rem;background:#e6eceb}.making-size p{margin:.5rem 0;font-size:.9rem}.making-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.7rem;margin:1.5rem 0 1rem}.chapter-making :global(.making-source){display:flex;align-items:start;gap:.65rem;font-weight:400;margin:.7rem 0}.chapter-making :global(.making-source input){width:1.1rem;height:1.1rem;flex:none;margin-top:.25rem}.chapter-making :global(.making-record){padding:.8rem 0;border-top:1px solid #cec9c1}.chapter-making :global(.making-record p){white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.chapter-making :global(.making-warning){border-left:3px solid #8a6a1f;padding-left:.75rem}.chapter-making [hidden]{display:none!important}.chapter-making button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #065e73;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.making-actions .studio-button{width:100%}}</style>

